OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1793370445
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G2/3
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Wed 4 Nov to Fri 13 Nov
OL,6,FHigh pressure is set to dominate
OL,7,Facross the UK early in this period,
OL,8,Fbringing a lot of dry weather. Some
OL,9,Fplaces may start foggy, this slow to
OL,10,Fclear, possibly even lingering all
OL,11,Fday. Elsewhere, cloud amounts will be
OL,12,Fvariable, but there should be some
OL,13,Fsunshine. Cloud may be thick enough at
OL,14,Ftimes for a little light drizzle
OL,15,Fthough. For most, temperatures are
OL,16,Flikely to be close to normal for the
OL,17,Ftime of year, though it will be chilly
OL,18,Fwhere any fog lingers. Some overnight
OL,19,Ffrost is likely where skies are clear
OL,20,Fand winds remain light. As we head
OL,21,Finto the following week, there are
OL,22,Fsigns that more unsettled weather may
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Freturn, but confidence surrounding
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Fthis change is low.
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
PN,16303
SC,0003
CT,20,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1793370445
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G3/3
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Fri 13 Nov to Fri 27 Nov
OL,6,FDuring the second half of November,
OL,7,Fthere is an increasing chance of more
OL,8,Funsettled conditions developing, which
OL,9,Fwould mean spells of rain and the
OL,10,Fpotential for strong winds at times.
OL,11,FThe extent and location of the wettest
OL,12,Fand/or windiest areas are uncertain at
OL,13,Fthis range, but the wettest and
OL,14,Fwindiest conditions are most likely in
OL,15,Fthe north and west, with relatively
OL,16,Fdrier conditions towards the south and
OL,17,Feast. Overall, temperatures will
OL,18,Fprobably be near or a little above
OL,19,Fnormal for the time of year.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
